<h1>AI agent inputs</h1>
<p>The AI agent needs these inputs. None of them is written specially for it.</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Input</th>
      <th>Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>The suite repositories</td>
      <td>The tests, groups and suites the AI agent may run, cloned where it works. Their config
        classes tell it which fields exist, which of them are endpoints and which are required.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>The endpoints file</td>
      <td>The machines and their addresses, saved from the controller's Endpoints panel. See
        <a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/endpoints/">Endpoints file</a>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>This documentation</td>
      <td>This section tells the AI agent how to configure a run, run it and read the log. The
        <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/">Framework reference</a> describes the classes and
        fields it writes. The instructions file below lists the addresses of both.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>A required field whose value is not in the code, such as the folder of a tool package, needs its
  value given as well. Otherwise the AI agent asks for it.</p>

<h2 id="instructions">Instructions file</h2>
<p>The practical arrangement is to keep all of this in the instructions file that the AI agent reads
  at the start of every request, such as <code>CLAUDE.md</code> or <code>AGENTS.md</code>. The file
  sits in the folder the AI agent works from, which holds the suite repositories and the run folder
  side by side. The template below is written for a machine where everything sits under
  <code>~/orcraft/</code>. The Rules section applies everywhere as written. Replace every line of the
  Paths section with your own.</p>

{% set agentInstructions %}
# Orcraft

An Orcraft test suite is ordinary Python. The same files run from the controller GUI, from the CLI, from CI and from an AI agent.
{% for section in docsSections %}{% if section.docsBase == "/ai-agents/" or section.docsBase == "/framework/" %}
